    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nSherry FitzGerald Conor McManus are pleased to bring to the market Cavanagarvan, Stranooden, Co. Monaghan. \n\nAn impressive detached residence enjoying a delightful countryside setting within close proximity of the village of Corcaghan.\n\nThe property occupies a generous, mature site surrounded by rolling countryside and enjoys a wonderful sense of space and privacy. A sweeping tarmac driveway leads to the residence, with extensive lawns surrounding the property and an integral garage providing additional practicality. \n\nThe spacious accommodaion comprises, an entrance hall, living room, sitting room, kitchen/dining room with adjoining sunroom, utility room, shower room/WC, home office and integral garage. Upstairs there are four well-proportioned bedrooms, (two ensuite), bathroom, dressing room and hot press.\n\nThe generous proportions and versatile accommodation make this an excellent family home.\n\nThe location offers the best of country living while remaining convenient to everyday amenities. St Michael's National School, community centre, local pub/eatery and church are all located nearby, making this an especially appealing setting for family life.\n\nA spacious family residence, combining generous accommodation, substantial grounds and an attractive rural setting.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nBright and welcoming entrance hall featuring wooden flooring and an impressive staircase with gallery-style landing above.\n\nLiving Room: - \nGenerously proportioned and bright living room featuring wooden flooring and a marble fireplace with gas fire. A large front-facing window provides excellent natural light and a pleasant outlook over the surrounding grounds.\n\nSitting Room: - \nSpacious and inviting sitting room featuring wooden flooring and an attractive ornate fireplace with cast-iron inset, complemented by a large front-facing window providing excellent natural light.\n\nSun Room: - \nBright sunroom overlooking the surrounding gardens and countryside. Wooden flooring and double doors provide a seamless connection to the adjoining kitchen/dining area.\n\nKitchen Dining Room: - \nGenerously proportioned kitchen/dining room fitted with an extensive range of solid wood units, integrated appliances and tiled flooring. Ample space is provided for family dining, with double doors opening directly to the adjoining sunroom.\n\nUtility Room: - \nPractical utility room fitted with a range of storage units, worktop space and sink, with plumbing for laundry appliances.\n\nGuest Shower Room: - \nConvenient ground-floor shower room comprising a spacious shower enclosure, pedestal wash hand basin and WC.\n\nMaster Bedroom: - \nGenerously proportioned master bedroom with feature bay window, wooden flooring and pleasant countryside views. Complete with a separate dressing room and private ensuite.\n\nDressing Room: - \nSpacious dressing room located off the master bedroom, with wooden flooring, fitted shelving and hanging space.\n\nEn-Suite: - \nSpacious ensuite comprising corner bath, separate shower enclosure, WC and wash hand basin, with wooden flooring and Velux rooflight providing natural light.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nBright and spacious double bedroom with wooden flooring and the benefit of a private ensuite shower room.\n\nEn-Suite: - \nEnsuite comprising shower enclosure with electric shower, WC and wash hand basin, with wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nBright and spacious bedroom with wooden flooring and large window enjoying pleasant countryside views.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nSpacious double bedroom with wooden flooring. A large window overlooking the surrounding countryside.\n\nBathroom: - \nSpacious family bathroom comprising large shower enclosure, WC and wash hand basin with fitted vanity unit and tiled flooring.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Total floor area: 239 sq. mts. ( 2573 sq ft ) approximately</li><li>Site area: 0.32 HA ( 0.8 acres ) approximately</li><li>Generous accommodation </li><li>Set on a spacious, mature site surrounded by open countryside</li><li>Sweeping tarmac driveway with ample private parking</li><li>Extensive lawns surrounding the residence</li><li>Integral garage</li><li>Excellent storage throughout</li><li>Attractive rural setting with pleasant countryside views</li><li>Convenient to St. Michael's National School, community centre, church and local pub</li><li>Within easy reach of Corcaghan village and Monaghan town</li><li>Oil fired central heating</li><li>Broadband available</ul>"
